CloudBurrow patch 8 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1061; the bug: #1122).

The bug: a function named by one quoted path, ``SELECT `project.dataset.fn`(3)``
or ```dataset.fn`(3)``, failed "Function not found", and a table function
so "Table-valued function not found", although BigQuery takes a routine's
name so (its user-defined functions guide writes CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION
`project.dataset.masking_routine1`(ssn STRING)) and the catalog already
registers a table under its whole dotted path. The patch registers a
function and a table function under the whole dotted path of each suffix
too, as addTableSpecRecursiveImpl does for a table.
function_by_quoted_path_test.go fails without the patch and passes with it.

